      origins: "Rummy games first appeared in the early twentieth century. Two main theories: Mexican origin from Conquian (first attested 1852), or Asian from a Mahjong-related game such as Kun P'ai. The draw-and-discard principle with melding appears in Chinese card games from the 18thâ€“19th century. The name 'rummy' may derive from British slang ('rum' = odd), Rum Poker, or the drink.",
