      timeline: [
        '1852: Conquian first attested in Mexico.',
        "1900s: Name 'Rummy' appears; game spreads in USA.",
        '1909: Gin Rummy variant created (Elwood Baker).',
        '1910sâ€“1920s: Rummy popular in USA and UK; Gin Rummy booms during Prohibition.',
        '1940sâ€“1950s: Canasta emerges from Uruguay.',
        'Present: Indian Rummy (Paplu) and online platforms flourish.',
      ],
      evolution: 'Basic Rummy (Straight Rummy) is the simplest form. Gin Rummy, 500 Rummy, Canasta, and Indian Rummy are major variants. Basic Rummy uses one draw, optional meld/lay-off, one discard; no requirement to meld before laying off on others in the standard rules.',
      cultural: 'A staple of home and club play. Gin Rummy was associated with Hollywood and Prohibition-era America. Indian Rummy is widely played online.',
    },
